      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems complicated, and also fairly fragile — what happens if some other process on the system (for example, a test running in parallel for a completely different package) dials the listener\u0027s port while the test is running?\n\n(Compare the approach taken in CL 184157 to obtain a pair of connected net.Conns.)\n\nPerhaps instead the listener could run as a loop, with the client setting the client address. Maybe something like:\n\n\tlistener, err :\u003d netListener()\n\tif err !\u003d nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"netListener: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tlistenerDone :\u003d make(chan struct{})\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\tlistener.Close()\n\t\t\u003c-listenerDone\n\t}()\n\n\tvar serverErrs sync.Map  // client address → chan error\n\tgo func() {\n\t\tdefer close(listenerDone)\n\t\tfor {\n\t\t\tc, err :\u003d listener.Accept()\n\t\t\tif err !\u003d nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\terr \u003d ServeAgent(keyringAgent, c)\n\t\t\terrc, _ :\u003d serverErrs.LoadOrStore(conn.RemoteAddr().String(), make(chan error, 1))\n\t\t\terrc \u003c- err\n\t\t\tc.Close()\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\t\n\ttestCase :\u003d func(t *testing.T, requestBytes []byte, wantServerErr bool) {\n\t\tc, err :\u003d net.Dial(\"tcp\", listener.Addr().String())\n\t\tif err !\u003d nil {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"net.Dial: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\t_, err \u003d c.Write(requestBytes)\n\t\tif err !\u003d nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Println(\"write error?\", err)\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Unexpected error writing raw bytes on connection: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\terrc :\u003d serverErrs.LoadOrStore(c.LocalAddr().String(), make(chan error, 1))\n\t\tserverErr :\u003d \u003c-errc\n\t\tc.Close()\n\t\tif serverErr \u003d\u003d nil {\n\t\t\t…\n\t\t} else if (serverErr !\u003d io.EOF) !\u003d wantServerErr {\n\t\t\t…\n\t\t}\n\t}",
      "revId": "cdf02f0d0428afc70811bbcc497be5505b199269",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
